Looking at the code, I found a clear bug in `TestSnapshotCases.java`.

```json
{
  "comments": [
    {
      "path": "x-pack/qa/repository-old-versions-compatibility/src/javaRestTest/java/org/elasticsearch/oldrepos/TestSnapshotCases.java",
      "start_line": 20,
      "end_line": 24,
      "content": "The ES_VERSION_6 constants are incorrectly set to version 5 values. `ES_VERSION_6` is `\"5\"` (should be `\"6\"`) and `ES_VERSION_6_STANDARD_TOKEN_FILTER` is `\"5_custom_analyzer\"` (should be `\"6_custom_analyzer\"`). This means RestoreFromVersion6IT and RestoreFromVersion6CustomAnalyzerIT (and the corresponding Mount tests) will actually restore the v5 snapshots instead of v6, so the v6 snapshot zips (snapshot_v6_custom_analyzer.zip) are never exercised. The comments also incorrectly say \"Index created in vES_5\"."
    }
  ]
}
```
